a health zone)","evidence":"Likasi is under normal state administration; PNC policing with FARDC support, including curfew enforcement (Feb 2025) and joint anti-banditry operations into 2026. Urban banditry is reported but no non-state group controls any neighbourhood; Bakata Katanga activity is in remote areas, not the city.","unit":"CD7106-likasi","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-fardc","role":"present"},{"entity_id":"bakata-katanga","role":"raiding"}],"source_ids":[172,178,186]},{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"medium","basis":"default_state_presence","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Peri-urban villages in Likasi city limits: Kampemba 1/2, Kampemba (Kakontwe HA), Buluo (Panda/Kambove health zones)","evidence":"No reported armed-group activity in these villages adjoining Likasi; nearest reported 2026 armed attack was in Luisha sector ~67 km away. Assessed as default state (PNC) presence.","unit":"CD7106-likasi","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-fardc","role":"present"}],"source_ids":[187]}],"sources":{"172":{"url":"https://fr.allafrica.com/stories/202601140048.html","title":"Lubumbashi - 7 présumés bandits et deux femmes arrêtés dans le cadre de l'opération Ndobo","publisher":"AllAfrica","date":"2026-01-14"},"178":{"url":"https://actualite.cd/2024/12/16/haut-katanga-face-la-recrudescence-de-linsecurite-urbaine-la-police-lance-lalerte","title":"Haut-Katanga : face à la recrudescence de l'insécurité urbaine, la police lance l'alerte","publisher":"Actualite.cd","date":"2024-12-16"},"186":{"url":"https://fr.allafrica.com/stories/202502240072.html","title":"Le gouverneur Jacques Kyabula prolonge le couvre-feu à Lubumbashi et Likasi pour 15 jours","publisher":"AllAfrica","date":"2025-02-24"},"187":{"url":"https://www.mediacongo.net/article-actualite-163457_double_attaque_meurtriere_a_luisha_l_igm_alerte_sur_la_montee_de_l_insecurite_dans_les_zones_minieres.html","title":"Double attaque meurtrière à Luisha : l'IGM alerte sur la montée de l'insécurité dans les zones minières","publisher":"Mediacongo","date":"2026-05"}},"units":{"CD7106-likasi":"Likasi, Haut-Katanga's second city and a copper/cobalt mining and rail hub, is firmly state-held and far from the eastern conflict zones. Daily order in its communes and health-area neighbourhoods is kept by the PNC, with FARDC garrisons in the city; provincial authorities imposed a night curfew on Lubumbashi and Likasi in February 2025 and police-army anti-banditry operations (e.g. Operation Ndobo) continued into 2026. Urban banditry and armed robbery are significant but no gang or militia holds territory. Bakata Katanga militia activity in 2025-2026 is reported in remote areas (e.g. Mitwaba/Upemba, Luisha sector ~67 km away), not in Likasi. Peri-urban villages (Kampemba, Buluo) have no reported armed-group activity and are assessed as default PNC presence."}}